!! Stride 2 Floor

Floor, wire and realm release shapes on the face and authority ground.

!!! Seven-league stride notes

* ''Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence). Its witness: a rotation-and-carry storm that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
* ''Research pair: the Keyhive substrate's contract'' (`W11`, filed after the seat). Its question: which substrate properties stand as contract and which shift by version, each needing a guard at run time. Lenses: dependency contract analysis / adversarial compatibility testing.
* ''Research pair: the knock's leak'' (`W10`; its answer moves the dial's bytes, so it lands before the bake). MEASURED (two traded rounds, then a Mu test on the web, 2026-10-26; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading): IK already stands, so a dialer proves itself before any verdict; the floor knock harms nothing the floor promises; on the sovereign route a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path learns which of the K gates sharing an address and route a dial selects, at most log2(K) bits per dial, never the face, the verdict or a sealed byte; no public-pin filter escapes that, and a secret selector costs per-Nexus key delivery and a causal re-key on every removal. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) that the sovereign promise leaves a pin-holding path reader outside it, so `W10` closes as a named leak, with more research owed later.

!!! The rows

* `W14` The floor card a banner carries in its `#floor=` link reads unsigned, on origin trust; a signed card stays owed. The floor read by release (`W26` slice 4) adds one rung and closes nothing here: a browser holding the Nexus AID verifies the epoch lineage, the head release and the floor bytes itself (`browser-floor-read`), anchored to the AID alone, since the genesis epoch re-derives it. The lineage rides the release record and the porch answer, never the card (a card holds 4096 characters, and the lineage self-certifies); that carrier changes nothing about trust, because the AID that anchors it comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins and never from the answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`floor-answer.test`). The AID itself still rides the same-origin trust line, and nothing proves the card's freshness: the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed for anchoring the AID and the card. W.
