<<~ ahu #/the-attractor>>

!! The attractor ~ what "done" reads as

The train closes when ''every surface of the superset publishes a row'' (`dreamdom#/the-superset`): its width, its root and sink, the control kinds and service kinds its manifest carries, and its result against the three conformance families (`filter-cts`, the camera goldens, the interaction goldens) with a named refusal wherever it has no road. Along the way:

* the first surface (the browser on the Node vessel's box) shows the daemon wiki, the pinned wiki and the other wikis as recipes or sleeping actors, and spawns each as the ordinary page template at the width the spike ruled;
* the browser DOM sink at width none loses no person's work: the six silent losses each pin to a green golden;
* one engine per wiki lives as an actor with a manifest, hibernates and wakes with its attachments, and refuses by name what its manifest lacks;
* a lean host (Mudlet, MCP) reads keys and writes records, and every act comes back named;
* the suite runs per host, and host drift (`Intl`, `localeCompare`, `Date`) shows on a published row before an operator meets it.

''Off the attractor by ruling'' (#/off-this-road): the syncer, the mutators, any authority on either side, a second evaluator, live 3D before the sensorium, UE6 before early access.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-order>>

!! The order ~ eight phases, one train

''The organizing law.'' The camera contract lands before any glass engine, so width none stays an honest fallback on every host; the record port lands before the glass engine, so the glass has records to replicate; the spike runs before the default width gets ruled; the actor wraps what stands rather than preceding it; conformance rides beside everything from D1 on, and no surface counts as landed without a row.

''The order'': D0 → D1 → D2 → D3 → D4, with D5 beside D1 onward and D6 after D2 and D5; D7 held by name.

!!! D0 · MEASURE AND MEND ~ what every phase needs (lane `dreamdom-harness`; the harness, the engine mends and the worker-side baseline stand; the rest stays owed here)
* ''Owed'': a second boot writing nothing, pinned over a staged vessel in e2e; a long-animation-frames observer on the current page (the house's own vessel page, beside the stock tab `measure:stock-tab` already observes; Chromium alone carries the observer, `dreamdom-field-scout` §6); heap after first paint for both instruments (D3's marginal-memory gate reads it). A burr for D3's spike: TiddlyWiki's `utils.timer` reads `window.performance` wherever `$tw.node` stands null, so `$:/config/Performance/Instrumentation` throws in the island until the forge lends a timer.
* ''Waits on'': nothing. ''Spikes'': none; this phase IS the instrument. ''Rulings'': none.

!!! D1 · THE CAMERA CONTRACT ~ the browser DOM sink at width none, hardened (lane `dreamdom-camera`; the contract, the island's camera, the page sink and every build below stand, with goldens 01 to 13 green on the engine and page harnesses; the rest stays owed here)
* ''Owed'': the whole-road Playwright run of the goldens over a staged vessel (the two harnesses stand in for it: the engine half over the fake document, the page half over the real sink with a stand-in island); `glass-switch-back-repaints` and `glass-print-refuses-by-name` as e2e witnesses; probes 2 and 4 of `page-controls#/measure-first`, and probes 1 and 5 in Gecko and WebKit; long animation frames across 100 edits on the vessel page (D0's observer); the page consuming the scroll and focus hints; `lar:disclosure-toggle` for disclosure state the wiki keeps; a `lar:breath` kind so the plate reads the island's breath after boot; the daemon surface's breath, custody and residency records (`daemon-surface#/the-talk-story`); the `data-lar-keys` stamp from `$edit-text`'s `parseKeyDescriptors`; the operator's own renames of `wiki:place-verb`, `daemon:*`, `cas:*` and `view:*`, deferred by their word.
* ''Builds'', whole: keyed frames with a per-key revision, a `membership` key, a `mountEpoch` and `sensedRevision[controlId]`, one whole-surface key first and the CSS as a key of its own (so a sheet crosses only when it changes, and the vessel's frame relay carries an absent key as absent); `lar:control-event` with `eventId`, `kind`, `seenFrameRev`, `localRev`, `wholeValue`, `modifiers`, `key` and as-of-act `geometry`; `lar:control-result` with `applied` · `stale-target` · `refused` and `want`; the answer ring per surface; declared cancellation and crossing (`data-lar-on`, `data-lar-cancel`, `data-lar-keys`, `data-lar-bubble`, `data-lar-live` descriptors) stamped by the patched `addEventListener` and a small per-widget table; the worker bubbling every type to the first listener and answering `unclaimed`; the serialiser promoting `checked` and `selected` to attributes at flush; `lar:resend` on `session:surface-open` and on switch; the island root-services startup module (`tm-rename-tiddler`, `tm-relink-tiddler`, `tm-home`, `tm-modal`, `tm-show-switcher`, `tm-notify`, `tm-scroll` and `tm-focus-selector` as hints) and `lar:service` with `lar:service-result` for clipboard, download, route and open-surface, each other kind refused by name with its alert; the three ruled page controls (`lar-field` through the editor's engine seam, `lar-popover`, `lar-disclosure`) and the page's per-control veto in `beforeNodeMorphed`; the IME rules (`keyCode 229`, one-task hold after `compositionend`, never morph a composing node); `lar-file-picker` and the page-side `import-offer` and `drop` with bounded bytes; `lar-order-list`; the document keyboard leg driven by a `shortcuts` key; the navigate service with the page composing `#` from the order key.
* ''Proves'': interaction goldens 1 to 13 (`dreamdom#/conformance`) green at width none over the DOM sink in Playwright, each red first; the five probes of `page-controls#/measure-first`; the three laws of `page-controls#/the-sinks-three-laws` kept; `glass-switch-back-repaints`; `glass-print-refuses-by-name`; the refusal words of `page-controls#/refusals` read beside the control in each engine.
* ''Measures'': serialised bytes per key and long animation frames across 100 edits beside the 11.7 KB plus 7.5 KB whole-frame number; a key splits (river frames plus order plus membership) only where that number asks (`dreamdom#/the-ruling`, measure first).
* ''Waits on'': D0's harness; `session-contract#/the-holder-protocol` for the envelope fields (builds against it; refuses `binding-unavailable` where a field has no holder yet).
* ''Spikes'': the declared-cancellation afternoon (#/the-spikes 1), serializer promotion (2), sensed revision end to end (3), the seam engine's toolbar (4), declared keys and the document leg (5), `import-offer` and `drop` (6), surface switch with epochs (7).
* ''Rulings'' (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`, ruled 2026-10-16): the stock edit template through the seam engine, each width naming what it cannot run; the root `tm-*` split, with `tm-http-request` as a gated door; `$eventcatcher` for declared discrete events and `$keyboard` with declared keys.

!!! D2 · THE RECORD PORT ~ inside the engine (lane `dreamdom-port`; its pure steps start beside D1)
* ''Builds'': the port's kinds on the live island: `port:open{wikiUri, width, since, actor, localFilter, renders[], edits, presence, maxRecordBytes, maxBatchBytes}`, `port:snapshot` (chunked), `port:changes` with cursors and tombstones, `port:write{txId, basis, records}` answered by `port:written` and echoed under `causedBy:[txId]`, `port:ask{kind: filter · render · load · verb · cas · invoke}` where `render` answers `html` · `text` · `blocks` (with `affordances[]`) · `label-html` and `invoke` carries a `renderCursor`, `port:presence` (lapse by presence rounds at causal boundaries, never persisted), `port:close`; the width field as a filter over fields on the engine side (cheap now, expensive to retrofit); the tier `localFilter` naming StoryList, HistoryList, `$:/state`, `$:/temp`, `$:/status` and `$:/info/browser/*`; a recording fakedom-style document and the blocks, text and label-html serialisers over it; the capability gate on every invoke before `invokeActions`.
* ''Proves'': the witnesses `dreamdom-port-contract` names, one red and one control each (the echo named by `txId`, the snapshot base, cursor resets, the whole-validated write with its retry and partial resume, presence by rounds, skinny then load, the tier-local titles, the invoke and verb gates, the `cas` tiers, the label-html and text serialisers); the blocks-sink parity run of interaction goldens 1, 2, 6 and 11 (headless, vitest) with the same expected writes and messages as the DOM sink; a missing camera degrades visibly.
* ''Observed'': the as-built cold read stands at `dreamdom-port-scout` and the field read at `dreamdom-port-field-scout`, each verbatim. The port's kinds join the island unions in `island-protocol.ts` beside the camera's; `port:ask` and the invoke gate sit in the island's dispatch (`wiki-behavior.ts`); `port:write` rides the outbound record path under its own `txId`. Four slices touch no shared file and open the lane: the recording document with its serialisers, the width and local-filter core, the invoke gate, and presence expiry.
* ''The contract'' stands ruled at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-port-contract">>: the five questions the field raised (snapshot base, cursor reset, the atomic write boundary, tombstone retention, clockless presence) and the invoke gate, each with its red and control; the rows owed beside the port stand there.
* ''Waits on'': D0. The serialisers wait on nothing; `blocks` for memetic-wikitext specifically waits on the Annex B widget-tree pass (D5).
* ''Spikes'': the blocks sink over a recording document (#/the-spikes 8); the synchronous ask on Node (`Atomics.wait` plus `receiveMessageOnPort`, bounded waits only).
* ''Rulings'' (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`, ruled 2026-10-16): presence at width none travels as a separate droppable message. The port ships with `causedBy` mandatory and skinny behind a flag.
* ''Stands'' (PR #87, 2026-10-23): the worker half: the port log, the wire, the island handler, one island to one face with a moved face retiring its port, the bounds, the composer lends and the holder's routes dropped by name until a port lease. Owed before D3: the composer wiring and the page transport, so no glass engine reaches a port yet, and the ledger slot a retired port's landed write keeps until its actor resends.
* ''The seventh silent loss'' (measured 2026-10-23; `dreamdom#/what-a-sink-keeps`): a reload soon after Confirm lost the edit, the island's loop stalled by a whole-corpus coherence refold. Lane `dreamdom-rest-before-reload` cures it ahead of D3: a per-title stalk memo, the browser rest door with heads (a stalled rest named, never silent), the page's unload hold while a reliable act waits, and the island owning the modified-click rule the stall had hidden. The remaining whole-corpus fold stays an owed row.

!!! D3 · THE GLASS ENGINE AND THE WIDTH SPIKE ~ full, skinny and story behind a flag (lane `dreamdom-glass`; waits on D1 and D2)
* ''Builds'': a port adaptor as a startup module on the glass that binds `$tw.wiki`'s `change` event, lands `port:changes` under an origin tag its own listener skips, posts `port:write` with `txId` and keeps the write optimistic until `port:written` echoes; no `$tw.syncer` constructed and no `syncadaptor` module shipped; the glass boot from the same CAS core blob by hash; the page template over `window.document` mounted in-process as the browser's first camera; skinny and story as settings of the same adaptor; `lar:service` doors reached from the glass engine's root handlers; the multi-tab topology (a Web Lock elects the leader, the leader's worker holds the engine, a SharedWorker or a BroadcastChannel handshake routes other tabs, a late tab gets a snapshot and never a missed `ready`); peer write into an open draft shown with the newer-base prompt; `§9` of `packages/AGENTS.md` reworded on the operator's ruling.
* ''Proves'': the full-width walk of the five `isTiddlyWikiFakeDom` sites in a real browser (`FramedEngine` inside the shadow root, storyviews, popup positioning, the toolbar, auto-height) before any default gets ruled; `glass-peer-edit-presence-reads-aloud`, `glass-skinny-body-loads-on-open`, `glass-echo-lands-once`, `glass-leader-handoff-mid-write`, `glass-late-tab-gets-snapshot`; interaction goldens 1 to 13 at width full with stock TW5 as oracle, which also certifies the goldens themselves.
* ''Measures'' (the separating experiment): one 2,000-tiddler corpus, one loopback port, the same glass booted at full, skinny and none (story only if skinny and full split), on the reference phone and on Node: heap after first paint; warm first paint; p95 keystroke-to-paint; the cold filter over tiddlers the glass never held; the peer write into the open editor; echo (exactly one write, zero re-landings); hot-swap to a second wiki and back; the synchronous ask on Node; the verb census (every worker-side verb that invoked a filter or a render); bytes per key at none. Thresholds: skinny loses if the cold filter exceeds 100 ms p95 on the phone or a `lazy-all` hole reproduces without a closable fix; full loses only on the marginal-memory gate (+25 % over a stock tab; a 150 MB tripwire); none loses if bytes per key exceed the 50 ms input budget on the phone after the key split, or if any ruled control fails its browser and accessibility probes.
* ''Waits on'': D1 (so none stands as the honest fallback) and D2 (so the glass has a port).
* ''Spikes'': the three-boot width spike (#/the-spikes 9); the full-width walk (10).
