* `D3` `lar:control-event` with an id and `lar:control-result` with a status; the answer ring; the reliable and droppable classes. D1. Stands (measured 2026-10-19); lead: the page re-sends no reliable act after a lost answer, so a dropped answer under one `eventId` owes its red.
* `D4` Declared cancellation, crossing keys and bubbling stamped at binding; the serializer promotion (`checked`, `selected`, `indeterminate`) with the toggle family green on both halves of golden 06; the textarea revert and the blanket cancel green. D1. Their rulings stand (2026-10-16). Stands in part (measured 2026-10-19): the table, the toggles, `indeterminate` and goldens 01, 03 and 06 stand; `$edit-text` declares no `keys` and `$browse` sits outside the table. The tail stands (PR #66): `$browse` joins the table, and `$edit-text` declares the chords its toolbar names, an editor with no toolbar declaring none.
* `D5` The island root-services module and `lar:service` with named refusals, golden 12 green on both runners; `lar:resend` and epochs on switch, golden 13 green on both. D1. Its ruling stands (2026-10-16). Stands (measured 2026-10-19).
