* `D10` The actor's manifest, gate, states, attachments, wake-on-act and recipe refusal; `worker-trust` retired. D4. Their rulings stand (2026-10-16).
* `D11` `filter-cts.json` reviewed and pinned; the `html` and `text` goldens on three hosts. D5. The `core` charter stays open. Stands (PR #63): 254 reviewed cases over the frozen world `pono-small` and the `html` and `text` camera goldens on Node and Chromium; quickjs-ng stays owed. Measured there: in a single-file wiki the standalone plugin carries the title `$:/plugins/lares/memetic-wikitext`, so `[all[memes]]` answers nothing on that host. A host-bound case compares against the world it names (PR #74): its parse tree stays whole and its result keeps only the titles that world owns, so a rebuilt plugin moves no locus while a drifted world title still reds.
