14:role      = "carriage-fold-lane — the lane kit a fresh local session takes for roadmap row `W18`: the founding hearth reads its carried herms' floor pins as `place-uncarried` in the held-out herm-mesh and nexus cells, so a host reader never files a herm's pin. It names the evidence measured so far, the causes ruled out with what ruled them out, the leading lead and the probe that settles it, the lane's branch and crucible under `mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`, its crew, its fences, where the evidence rests on disk, and who answers questions while the controller's session stays open."
40:!! The evidence ~ measured, with where each reading rests
49:So the herms count the carries from their bundles and read every pin, while A's running daemon sees the pin statements and counts none of the carries it wrote. `place-uncarried` names exactly `carriers.has(placeKey)` failing after the statement's signature, Nexus, route and tier passed (`place-floor-pin.ts`).
53:# ''A head-only fold after a charter roll.'' `foldCarrierSet` runs without ancestry at three sites (the pull in `herm-carriage.ts`, `placeArmFor`, `placeCarriedNexuses`), so a carry at a closed epoch would read uncarried. Measured in a test that walks the container's own order (the boot's charter roll in `tools/lararium-container-boot.sh`, then four `carry-for → carry → carry-take` joins): A's head epoch and all four carries share one epoch, and A files all four pins (Sol, round 4).
56:''The leading lead (inferred, unmeasured).'' The in-process reproduction holds one Repo; the container does not. In A's container, `nexus carry` runs as a separate CLI process that writes the carriage board into the store on disk, while A's long-running daemon reads the board through a live handle it materialized once and caches per url. The herms' own pin statements reach the daemon over the network; the CLI's carry acts may never reach the daemon's live document. That fits the split: pins seen, carries not counted.
58:''The probe that settles it.'' In a two-process test (a running daemon composition and a separate `nexus carry` writing the same store), or in the container itself, read the carriage board through the daemon's live handle after the CLI's carry and compare it with the store on disk. If the daemon's handle lacks the carry acts, the cure belongs where a CLI write reaches a running daemon (the verb seat over the UDS socket, or the daemon reloading a board another process changed); if it holds them, the fold or the reader is the next suspect.
66:* ''Branch'': `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--carriage-fold`, cut from the work branch's head after the controller's settle push. Nothing lands on the work branch directly.
67:* ''Crew'' (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes`): the session leads as the Opus Episkopos; the work swarm's Sol and Luna build pair builds in ONE provisioned worktree (operator, 2026-10-18; `mixed-model-swarm#/the-shapes`) (`node tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>`), coordinating through `.lane-claims.md`; the Copilot Chao pair (Hodge, Podge, the Spin) and an Opus overwatch read the burst; the lane closes with an o-takiage pass (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-otakiage`).
69:* ''The crucible'' (`mixed-model-swarm#/the-lanes`): push the lane branch (its CI and held-out run there, and the held-out herm-mesh and nexus cells are this lane's witness), open a pull request into the work branch, answer every comment (a Copilot PR review runs only on the operator's ask), then the controller merges.
80:* `held-out-herm-mesh-artifact/`: the cell's own logs (`mesh-compose.log` holds every container's lines; `driver.log` the witness).
94:# ''Fetch first.'' Cut the lane branch from the work branch as origin holds it after the controller's settle push; confirm the settle's commits (the dist guard, `mixed-model-swarm`, this kit) stand in it.
95:# ''Provision, never link.'' The dist guard refuses a worktree whose `node_modules` link into another checkout; `node tools/provision-worktree.mjs <empty-dir>` gives the build pair one worktree with its own links and builds. A provisioned worktree initializes submodules, so its removal at the lane's close waits on the operator's `--force`.
96:# ''Write the probe before any cure.'' Four diagnostic rounds produced two plausible cures that measurement refuted; the cross-process lead stands inferred until a red test reproduces A refusing pins it holds carries for.
98:# ''Spend Copilot on purpose.'' The Chao pair on cheap models reads each burst; a Copilot PR review runs only on the operator's ask; a deeper eye runs only on a KAIROS pull the operator hears first.
