44:''Kalani's two tabs.'' Kalani wears two faces in one browser: their own, and the Teshima Family Council's. One tab stands unlocked as the Council; the other tab still asks for Kalani's own unlock. The Council tab writes a family recipe. Today one holder serves both tabs, and a sealed write could reach a sealer that holds keys for both faces. After Wave B, the Council tab's write goes to the Council's sealer alone, under the Council's own row-class key, and the locked tab's port receives nothing sealed at all: the holder never admitted that port's session. When Kalani closes the Council tab, the last Council session closes, and the Council's hive locks, while Kalani's own face stays as it stood.
46:''The stranger's port.'' A script in some other page opens a port to the holder and asks for a sealed body. The holder knows no session that port opened, so it refuses by name and answers nothing more. No face's key ever meets that port.
48:''The node, isomorphic by intent.'' A node vessel wears the same two faces on one daemon. Its sessions and registries route by face too: the Council's bag-doc ledger, grant record and registry live on the Council's own plane, and no union registry spans both faces. A session that wears the Council reads Kalani's rows nowhere, and the reverse holds.
50:''The mythic view.'' Each family keeps its fire in its own clay pot now (the atom cut). Wave B builds the doors: each pot sits behind a door that opens only for a family member who stands in the room, the room empties and the door shuts, and a voice from the street gets no answer. The place keeps its lamp at the gate for strangers to see by, and nothing more.
58:# ''Chunk zero, the cut's own debts.'' Five passages of law the atom cut's rewording dropped return in the atom's wording (the group born under the atom and why the place never creates it; the pinned KEL prefix as the boot's root; no fallback reading for a bare edge; a cardless vessel never speaks at a gate; an uncommitted founding belongs to no face). The roster law gets its witness: the place stands on no face's roster after a founding, an admit and a fleet join, against a planted control. ''Isomorphic by intent'': one face-atom custody contract in the mesh, keyed by PersonaGroup, each host supplying only its row store; its red first, a node holding face A that joins face B's fleet presenting A's atom as B's (one key on two rosters), where the browser already keys by group. The admit's archive guard lifts into keyhive for both hosts. ''Idempotent by intent'': the atom stands or keeps (mint when absent, the same bytes a no-op, other bytes refused by name), where the node writes blind.
59:# ''The scout census first.'' The lead's first act reads, writes nothing: every site where a session, a registry or a sealer reaches more than one face (a union), on node and browser alike, named by file and line, sorted by what inherits shape from what. The Sol scouts the node half and the Copilot the browser holder, in parallel and read-only, and each cross-reads the other's census; the lead merges one census before any build.
60:# ''The isolation red, on real routes'' (`K15`'s own red, now past the row level): unlock face A alone, bypass every router, session and UI, and try to open and replace face B's occupied rows with every key A holds; each open fails and B's bytes stand unchanged. Its control: the same act as B, unlocked, opens.
61:# ''One face per session, no union'' (`K15` step 3): each session and registry routes by its one face; a union site from the census reads red until it routes by face. Control: a single-face vessel reads byte-identical before and after.
62:# ''The asker seals'' (`F6` slice three, ruling (a′)): the Repo lives in the holder, and a sealed write goes to the asking tab's face sealer, under that face's row-class key. Red: a write from face A's tab reaches a sealer that holds B's key. Control: A's write opens under A.
63:# ''The admit guard'' (`B1`): the holder answers a port only for a session it admitted. Red: an unadmitted port asks for a sealed body and receives anything but a refusal by name. Control: an admitted port of the same face receives its body.
64:# ''The last session locks'' (`B1`): the last session of a face to close locks that face's hive. Red: after the last close, a sealed read under that face opens. Control: while another session of that face stands, it still opens.
66:Each red lands as its own commit, red on that commit, before its cure; each control rides with its red. A red that passes on its red commit measures nothing: the lead proves the instrument with a known positive first.
74:''We work in very large work chunks under the mixed-model-swarm protocols'' (operator, 2026-10-19). Wave B runs as ONE joint lane, one sub-branch (`feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--k15-wave-b`) and one pull request, tested whole once, merged by train. It does not split into a PR per slice; the lead lands the reds and cures as commits in grounds-before-wins order and hands the lane back once.
77:* ''Two enacting seats'': one Codex Sol-6, launched as the walled Codex spirit (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">> #/the-launch), and one Copilot `gpt-5.3-codex` at medium effort through `launch-copilot-builder.sh` (a read through `launch-copilot.sh`). Both build in the ONE worktree the lead provisions (`node tools/provision-worktree.mjs <dir>`), coordinating through its claims ledger (`.lane-claims.md`): claim a path before writing it, release it once it stands, never write a path the other holds. Each seat builds or reads as the work pulls, and a seat never reads a diff it wrote. Sol and `gpt-5.3-codex` share the OpenAI lineage, so their cross-read counts once; the Episkopos reads every build as the second lineage.
