31:!! The mandate (operator rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22)
33:* ''One lease law.'' Every lease epoch rises only on a signed advance. A face advances by a per-writer signed slot under its KEL lineage. A Nexus or cabal-realm advance signs as a `QuorumAct` at the roster's threshold under its own epoch's lineage.
44:# ''R2 ~ the writer on held seats ~ BUILT.'' The `nexus-rekey` verb resolves the resource's own charter (`lease-charter.ts`: a Nexus AID, or a realm through the Nexus its ledger names), takes the held seats at the threshold (`selectHeldQuorumSigners`) and lands the advance through `rollQuorumLeaseOnBoard`. Fewer held seats refuse by name; the vessel's atom signs nothing here.
47:# ''R5 ~ the realm boards' frontiers ~ BUILT.'' `realm-frontier.ts` rides the shared hand frontier (`fleet-frontier.ts`) for the charter quorum and for each voucher. The quorum signs genesis and each successor; a voucher's own hand (`holder:<key>`, one key, one epoch) registers its genesis at its vouch and its raises with each act it signs. A quorum act registers its raise in the same board change (`edge-kapae-cmd`); a seated vouch founds the quorum genesis on first touch where this vessel holds the threshold of seats.
48:** ''The roll registers its head.'' The roll anchor signs each anchored realm's head under the lineage that includes the rolled epoch, in the same board change as the anchor (`runEdgeRollAnchors` takes the rolled `SealEpoch`); the two-vault anchor partial carries the opener's frontier signatures, and the cosigner lands anchor and head together once they stand at the threshold.
49:** ''A split-seat cosign carries its head.'' The opener's partial carries the frontier it signs (`frontier-carry.ts`); the cosigner checks it against what it would sign itself, adds its seats, and lands act and head in one change. A partial that needs a head and carries none refuses `frontier-missing` below the threshold.
50:** ''The admit bundle carries the board's frontier.'' `realmAdmitBundle` (invite, the Nexus claim, the quorum's and the voucher's frontier records and snapshots) rides out of `cabal vouch` and into `cabal join --bundle`; a joiner holding no copy of the realm's boards acts as of the carried head, which counts only where it verifies under the charter that joiner holds.
51:** ''Readers.'' The shadow ring reads every hand (`RealmFold.frontier`, `RealmFold.holders`): `memberAside` answers aside and `standsInRealm` false where the quorum frontier does not qualify, and a vouch whose voucher's hand does not qualify counts for nobody. `cabal-join` waits as `frontier-unknown` before an admission and names the head it acted under (`frontier.asOf`).
53:!!! Owed
56:Reds: an unsigned advance on a realm raises nothing and a threshold hand raises it (`quorum-lease.test.ts`, `lease-rekey.test.ts`); a sub-threshold hand raises nothing; an older epoch's advance verifies under its own epoch's keys and a forged lineage refuses; a realm reader before any qualifying frontier waits as unknown and acts as of it after (`realm-frontier.test.ts`, `edge-shadow-ring.test.ts`); the census proves itself on a planted site.
FILE:/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane.mem
10:role      = "the W26 lane's kit: the architecture the operator's ruling of 2026-10-18 adopts (one owner per registry; the floor reads by CID), the evidence that drew it, the six slices in grounds-before-wins order, what each slice retires, and the crew and crucible a lead walks"
23:Roadmap row `W26` carries the build of two operator rulings: //the system wikis release; every other wiki reads the floor// (2026-10-16) and //one owner per registry; the floor reads by CID// (2026-10-18), both at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> #/rulings. Rows `W21` and `P8` ride it. The law it enacts already stands at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/wiki-layer-ontology">> #/oracle-planes: an oracle names documents at one scope, that scope's owner writes its registry, and a registry travels no wider than its scope.
46:    @catalog            the operator's documents, at the operator's scope
57:''What the shape answers.'' The `lares` and `lararium` documents live in one place, the Kahu realm of the Nexus whose cabal writes them; on a lone hearth that realm belongs to its operator, who stands as its own Kahu. Every other vessel holds their snapshots by CID. A vessel's own pointers rest in its own bootstrap, so no shared document hosts another vessel's url and nothing merges across siblings. A wiki's floor moves only on a person's accept of a signed release, face by face, so one vessel may hold two Nexuses' floors and ties no face to another.
78:# ''The live system documents rest in the Kahu realm'', under persona zero's group until `K15`'s face context stands and the Kahu face's own group takes the seat (#/the-seam-owed-to-wave-c). A one-seat founding lands a counted 1-of-1 Kahu-cabal admission for persona zero's group; `kahuCabalCanonAccess` gains its production caller; `bags/` projects on the Kahu's vessel alone. The first red stands before any document moves, since no production path calls `kahuCabalCanonAccess` today (`kahu-cabal-admission.ts`): a one-seat founding reads system canon through it over a founded island. Then the red: a lone hearth's `working-loop` promotion lands, and a second vessel holds no live system document.
79:# ''The release answer.'' One porch body per Nexus, sealed by the steward under its own signing domain, `floor-release` (operator-approved, 2026-10-18), the promotion approval over the manifest's exact bytes attached; the crossroads board carries it; `P8` folds in. `ORACLE_POINTER_DOMAIN` retires once releases stand.
81:# ''Reach into system canon.'' Every residency verb into `bags/lares` or `bags/lararium` refuses a hand outside the Kahu cabal, through the one predicate slice 3 seats; the skipped red in `unbuilt-laws.test.ts` ("a non-Kahu MOVE into a canon bag refuses") greens here.
83:''Beside the slices.'' `herm-reshares-public-blob` re-aims onto a public user bag: it tests a herm's re-share of a public blob, and a peer's write into system canon belongs to the Kahu alone. The re-aim travels to the mesh-goldens lane as a patch, beside the layer instrument that measured step ③.
87:<<~ ahu #/the-seam-owed-to-wave-c>>
89:!! The seam owed to Wave C ~ one accessor names the Kahu realm's group
91:`kahuRealmGroup` (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/kahu-canon-reach.ts`) names the PersonaGroup that holds a Nexus's Kahu
92:realm. Persona zero's group holds it today. Wave C (`K15` step 6) swaps the Kahu face's own group in at that function
98:''THE LINEAGE RIDES THE RECORD, NEVER THE CARD.'' The release record and the porch answer carry the charter's epoch lineage, so a herm and a browser verify a release holding the Nexus AID alone. A card holds 4096 characters and the lineage self-certifies against the AID, so the card stays small. The carrier changes nothing about trust: the AID that anchors the lineage comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins, never from the same answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`foreign-nexus`).
100:''THE WIKI ISLAND TRUSTS THE GATE.'' A verb routed into a wiki island (`lares act --in-wiki`, `wiki-act`) carries its real
101:destination and source inside `args.args`, where the gate's cap derivation never looked. The keyholder island's
102:verify-then-delegate gate now asks the Kahu predicate for each system bag the envelope names (`routedInnerBags`,
103:`CapabilityVerifier.kahuReach`), before it routes. The wiki island holds no board and no sentinel, so its action reactors
104:run with `kahuReachClearedAtGate` and ask nothing again. The flag is a composition option set in code at the island's behavior, never a field of the envelope, so nothing a caller sends lifts it; every other composition leaves it unset and asks itself (`gateRoutedVerb`, `kahu-reach-gate-envelope.test`).
118:* RETIRED at slice 4: `OraclePointer`, `ORACLE_POINTER_DOMAIN`, `snapshotPublicOracle` and the node's oracle floor serve. The floor answers by the release at the porch; the flow map keeps its own pointer under `FLOW_POINTER_DOMAIN` (`flow-pointer`), and `oracle-substrate`, `oracle-read-client` and `oracle-read-face` live on as `flow-substrate`, `flow-read-client` and `flow-read-face`. Left for an o-takiage pass: the route and gate names that still say "oracle" (`ORACLE_SOCKET_ROUTE`, `OracleFloorGate`, `OracleGateArgs`), which name the flow map's socket and not a pointer.
121:''The interim cure stays out.'' The lane's recipe-watch hold (`--w26-own-canon`, commit `d1983aa75`) keeps a system wiki's own canon against a shared pointer that slice 2 removes; under //build the end state// it lands nowhere. Its probes stand: the shared-oracle probe as slice 2's red, the `W25` creator probe as that row's measurement.
125:<<~ ahu #/owed>>
127:!! Owed beside the slices
131:* ''A browser Kahu hand.'' The browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, so it fails closed on every system bag. A browser vessel holding the Kahu face rides Wave C's face context (`K15` step 6), which carries the charter and the board to it.
132:* ''A sibling device of a seat-holding face'' (the row beside the browser Kahu hand). A joined device is a sibling of the Kahu's own face, so by law its reach follows the face's counted admission once the charter's board reads on it. Today it composes no board source, reads as a stranger and draws `kahu-reach` on a system bag: a missing source, not the law. `e2e/meme-two-vessel-bag` step eight keeps the law's expectation (B promotes into its own lares book) as a `test.fails` named for this row, so it turns red the day the row lands and the lander flips it; `device-admit.ts` states the law.
134:* ''The floor card's freshness.'' The browser verifies the lineage, the head release and the floor bytes from the Nexus AID alone (`browser-floor-read`). The AID rides the same-origin trust line, and the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed.
145:* ''Shared ground'': both vessel composers. One lane at a time holds a composer hunk; the others hand theirs to the controller as a patch. Slice 1's re-bake and every plugin-bundle rebuild land on the controller's word.
146:* ''The crucible'': each touched package's whole suite under a scratch `HOME` and `LAR_ROOT`, `tools/typecheck-witness.sh`, one shard run with its `MERGE-VERIFY` line, a pull request into the span with no Copilot review unless the operator asks; the controller runs `tools/witness-all.sh` and merges.
