35:* ''Peers learn the head.'' Rows ride the Nexus carriage board under `PLACE_KEL_PREFIX` keyed by the inception AID (`place-kel-board.ts`), and the carry bundle carries them to an offline herm (`carry-bundle.ts`, `placeKel`). A reader pins the inception, `foldPlaceKel` verifies every digest, sequence, predecessor, reveal and cold signature to the head, and `acceptPlaceHead` holds it against the last accepted head. A gap, rollback or fork refuses advancement; the last accepted head stays "as of my last sync". A row that fails its own signature never advances a head.
36:* ''The framed duties.'' The five floor duties (carriage carrier, place floor pin, flow pointer, raise challenge, gate place finish) sign and verify one image `u32 len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` (`frameFloorDuty`, `floorDutyOf`, `verifyPlaceDuty`, `verifyPlaceDutyAtHead` in `place-signer.ts`). The KEL events sign under the KEL grammar, never a sixth floor domain.
37:* ''The seed census.'' `tools/seed-census.mjs` names every raw-seed consumer against an explicit list, proves itself on a planted consumer, and fails on any new consumer or stale entry. The K15 entries ride it as named owed exceptions in `{rule, file, match, count, reason}` shape, and K15 burns each when its bond lands.
50:# ''Built ~ the browser founding'' (`browser-vessel-identity.ts`: `foundBrowserPlaceKel`, `loadBrowserPlaceKel`, `readBrowserPlaceHead`). A leaf mints the armed inception through the same mesh grammar and reads its cold card back through the same `PlaceFoundingCard` port (`place-founding-card.ts` in mesh). A leaf holds no floor, so with no ceremony seated the identity open founds the device key and no KEL, and the explicit door refuses `PlaceFoundingCardUnread` until a ceremony UI seats a card (`placeFoundingCard` on `openBrowserVessel`). Heads read through the one `foldPlaceKel`.
54:# ''Owed ~ the readers by head.'' The four duty verifiers verify under the key a caller passes; the floor pin claim lane (W14 to W16) resolves each duty's signer through `verifyPlaceDutyAtHead`. Names that key a place by its inception key follow the head when that lane lands.
55:# ''Owed ~ the gate place finish.'' `gate-exchange.ts` already frames its image and did not move.
56:# ''Owed ~ K15's bonds.'' The vessel-wide Keyhive Individual and place card, the bare place leaf, the relay key, daemon auth, device and face work, internal asks and `lares meme` signing stay on the seed census as named K15 exceptions.
66:# A sixth signer domain, an embedded-domain trick, a cross-duty replay, an unframed image and an old key after rotation refuse; each of the five duties signs and verifies framed.

