/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:104:* ''The seventh silent loss'' (measured 2026-10-23; `dreamdom#/what-a-sink-keeps`): a reload soon after Confirm lost the edit, the island's loop stalled by a whole-corpus coherence refold. Lane `dreamdom-rest-before-reload` cures it ahead of D3: a per-title stalk memo, the browser rest door with heads (a stalled rest named, never silent), the page's unload hold while a reliable act waits, and the island owning the modified-click rule the stall had hidden. The remaining whole-corpus fold stays an owed row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:106:!!! D3 · THE GLASS ENGINE AND THE WIDTH SPIKE ~ full, skinny and story behind a flag (lane `dreamdom-glass`; waits on D1 and D2)
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:109:* ''Measures'' (the separating experiment): one 2,000-tiddler corpus, one loopback port, the same glass booted at full, skinny and none (story only if skinny and full split), on the reference phone and on Node: heap after first paint; warm first paint; p95 keystroke-to-paint; the cold filter over tiddlers the glass never held; the peer write into the open editor; echo (exactly one write, zero re-landings); hot-swap to a second wiki and back; the synchronous ask on Node; the verb census (every worker-side verb that invoked a filter or a render); bytes per key at none. Thresholds: skinny loses if the cold filter exceeds 100 ms p95 on the phone or a `lazy-all` hole reproduces without a closable fix; full loses only on the marginal-memory gate (+25 % over a stock tab; a 150 MB tripwire); none loses if bytes per key exceed the 50 ms input budget on the phone after the key split, or if any ruled control fails its browser and accessibility probes.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:112:* ''Rulings'' (`dreamdom#/open-rulings`): the `§9` wording and the confirm road's home per width stand ruled (2026-10-16); the default width of the first surface stays open until the three-boot spike reads. The flag ships first; the default flips after.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:114:!!! D4 · THE WIKI ACTOR ~ the lifecycle layer (lane `dreamdom-actor`; waits on D2; its manifest and gate may start beside D3)
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:115:* ''Builds'': one actor per wiki with an id, one writer and a manifest `{renders[], edits, presence, sensoria[], width[], maxRecordBytes, maxBatchBytes}`; the capability gate on the actor replacing `worker-trust` (admin-auth plus the keyhive check over `requestedBy`), so a lean invoke never bypasses authority; the states daemon · pinned · sleeping · recipe · spawned with their transitions; per-port attachments `{cursor, subscriptions, width, actorKey, localFilter, cameraMount}` serialised at hibernation and restored at wake; wake-on-act with one parked act per surface and a `waking` state beside the control, `superseded` for a second act, `actor-not-spawned` with a `spawn` affordance for a recipe; the holder's refusal to hibernate an actor holding an unanswered reliable act; the first surface's list of wikis by state; `tm-open-window` as `open-surface` (a second camera on the same actor); `$:/state` per surface or shared, by ruling; a warm start measured against `v8.startupSnapshot` in a `worker_thread`.
