/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom-roadmap.mem:199:* `D1` The second-boot-writes-nothing pin over a staged vessel, the vessel page's long-animation-frames observer and the heap-after-first-paint reading for both instruments. D0. Nobody owes a ruling. Measured 2026-10-19: the long-animation-frames observer stands on the stock tab alone (`stock-tab-baseline.ts`), no heap reading and no second-boot e2e stand, and the island emits `tm-scroll` and `tm-focus-selector` hints that no page code reads yet (`data-lar-scroll-to`, `data-lar-focus`). Stands in part (PR #66): the page reads the island's scroll and focus hints once per rising sequence, and the vessel page reports long-animation frames and heap after first paint or names each absent; the second-boot pin waits on `K15`'s per-face bag binding, its clock-named cap rows cured (PR #67). Leads: the long-animation-frame buffer grows for the page's whole life, and an invalid hint selector drops without a word.
