/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:537:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:538:* ''Integrity owed: the refold's bound'' (`G15`). Its witness: a roll storm that completes in bounded passes, one holder at a time, with no overlap and no starved holder.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:539:* ''Integrity owed: the habit flip at the bake'' (`X0`, `G37`). Before the bake the house runs re-genesis freely, since no CRDT document survives; after it, a re-genesis costs every CID a second operator pins. Its witness: a census of each instrument, fixture, brief and runbook line that assumes a free re-genesis, each named to flip or retire inside the bake's own commit, never after it.
