/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:543:* `G15` The refold's answers. For the compose owner, who holds `open-node-vessel.ts`: `after-roll-awaited.test.ts` reads source shape alone, and wants the chain lifted into a module a vector can run; an unbounded `afterRollChain` stage can stall later rolls, and a bound must never let two refolds of one holder overlap. Beside those: the plugin build's transcript records a fixed logical path for the TW5 binary, never the resolved one (`build-plugin-tiddler.ts`); its cure moves genesis attestation bytes, so it rides a labelled re-bake. G.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:544:* `G37` The evergreen sweep of 2026-10-18 (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/evergreen-sweep-2026">>, its six rulings and fourteen lanes). Built: (1) the standing witness `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` (PR #53), its ceilings version 59 (F6's envelope took five), clock 57 (the engine watch took two, the cap-event rows one) and narration 202 (W27 took one) over 1079 files; (8) the engine watch reads an engine by its sha256 (PR #60); (5) worldline replay orders by parent links and handle dependencies and names every skip (PR #62), the mempalace KG still dropping `parentKey` when it persists and the CLI tree's sequential mark still reading recorded times, each exception naming its rule, file, line, count and reason; (2) `bytesEqual`, `constantTimeBytesEqual`, a strict `hexToBytes` and `nexusAidOfPin` in `@lararium/mesh` (PR #51). Order of the rest: (3) opaque ids, the mount nonce, optional display times and parent-link worldline replay, after `W26` slice 2, the clock sinks at effect-record, residency-actions, sense-sensorium, handler-args, engine-watch, wiki-behavior, verb-tiddler and vessel-mailbox; (4) the engine watch by CID, the `LarDoc` and session-envelope shapes, the floor announcement's kind and the browser store's current shape; (5) the numbered preimages and formats renamed together in the bake that closes `W26`, the signing preimages outside `domains.ts` among them (holder-continuity, persistence-keel, wax-stamp's `lar-*/v1`), which take the same frozen-preimage ruling as `engine/v1`. Each lane red-first under a clock set to 1970 and to 3000. G.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:545:* `X0` The founding bake: one deliberate re-genesis before a second operator stands, after which CIDs are meant to last because another operator pins them. It moves together `K15` step 6 (identity bytes, split stores, slot trees and FCKs, archive and custody formats, each face's random device veil), the place KEL's pre-rotation and the scoped place signer (the signer frames each duty's domain itself, signing `len(D) ‖ D ‖ preimage` and its verifiers the same, so no signed floor image carries its own separation; built with `W29`, whose readiness red reads a fresh genesis founded armed, the five framed pairs verifying, and an old-shape inception refused by name, `old-shape-inception`), `W26`'s closing bake (the floor release), and `G37`'s preimage and format renames (`engine/v1` and its kin, the floor announcement's kind, the genesis seed and CAS formats). Each member carries its own readiness red, so the bake waits on the slowest by name, never on a date; the bake's own red: a fresh genesis founds, no CID from before the bake verifies after it, and a mixed old archive refuses by name. The gate it opens: a second operator may found a Nexus fresh at two of two. X.
