/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:572:* `A11` A pushed head of this branch whose held-out reading shows every driver green (`node tools/ci-verdict.mjs`, the third reading). A.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:573:* `A12` An unlock spends its time in three boots of the wiki engine, and the terminal shows nothing meanwhile. One instrumented run on a marked scratch root, pinned to one core, with the genesis corpus alone: the key derivation takes under two seconds; the sovereign composition then takes about six to reach `corpus-ready`, seven from the `[dyad]` line to the daemon island's `working layer attached`, and four to `tw5-booted`. An unlock sent while the floor's own daemon island still boots waits that boot out first, six seconds more, so the first unlock after a restart answered in twenty-eight seconds where a later one answered in fifteen. The span a person met past eighty seconds sits at the same `[dyad]` line, so it scales with the corpus the daemon island boots over. No small cure reads here. Owed: a progress line per phase at the unlocking terminal, and a measurement over a full workspace corpus. The compose owner's boot path. A.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:574:* `A13` A staged container that restarts after its boot's founding act wrote the seed charter and before it lit persona zero's face loses the staged card: the next boot's act completes the face, the charter already stands, so no card returns, and the kahu roll under `LAR_STAND_KAHU` skips with its warning (`tools/lararium-container-boot.sh`, the `LAR_STAND_FACE` founding and the roll after it). It binds disposable staged roots alone: a household founding prints its card on the terminal and keeps no copy. A.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:575:* `K8` The face-proof gate reads the admitted key's hand-over line, as the socket gate does. The key and its line stand built: a face's per-Nexus key mints at random into its sealed row and re-issues by a hand-over the carriage board carries (`nexus-leaf.ts`, `lares persona reissue`; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof#/the-key-hierarchy">>). The remainder rides the socket cutover. W.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:576:* `K13` The sealed outbox (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/custody#/the-table">>). Parcels rest sealed under random names in the `outbox` class. Owed: carriage shipping, idempotent receipt and local delete after ship. K.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:582:* `P18` The shared-canon read consults `kahuCabalCanonAccess`, admission AND sentinel membership; until it does, a removed group keeps its Keyhive sentinel capability at every reader but that one (`boot-daemon-keyhive`). Both vessels' daemon payloads (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`) carry the group and sentinel ids alone, so each composition threads the Nexus AID, the seated roster and the carriage board into the read together; a node-only gate leaves the browser reader open. P.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:583:* `P19` Cabal acts across a roll: an act counts only under the epoch it names, so after a seal roll standing reads `absent` until the seats re-admit at the new head; anchored ancestry, which `lares nexus members` reads, carries them, and an `onRolled` refold for the cabal verbs follows once a live reading folds them. It lands with `P20`, under the same writer rule. P.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:584:* `W10` The knock tests offline for a reader holding candidate pins and the clear path (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/gate-bundle.ts`, `knockSegment`, `gateKnock`): CLOSED as a named leak by the operator's ruling (2026-10-26), the sovereign route's promise leaving a pin-holding path reader outside it (face-proof #/named-leaks; the reading at `docs/pono/w28-gate-lane` #/the-knock-reading). More research owed later: whether a secret selector, its first-dial bootstrap and its causal re-key on every removal earn their cost, read again when a sovereign pin escapes its members' custody, when route confidentiality against pin-holders enters the promise, or when hearths commonly stand many Nexuses behind one address; a flip after `X0` moves the dial's URL bytes by its own versioned rite. W, canon.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:592:* `F1` The scoped document view stands specified in mesh (`session-document-view.ts` over `gated-sync-leg.ts`); the pool's surface door (`mountSurface`) and the island kernel's half ride it, and no production caller mounts a surface. Owed: every interactive surface mounts under it in place of the broad sync port, which waits on a verified face (train W) and on callers that hold a session (`F4`, `F6`); the share verdict's caller keeps an owner from offering a session island a document beyond its facets; an admitted leaf's relay adapter wears the one-way gate over its hearth's canon documents, and the hearth wears that gate's twin toward its leaves (`hearth-canon.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `open-node-vessel.ts`); a wiki island's verbs that read the catalog document move to the view's catalog ask. O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:593:* `F2` One recipe resolver (`surface-recipe.ts`) and the pool keyed by the whole session key (`mountSurface`) stand specified in mesh, with one proof through the node vessel's own parts that a recipe naming an offering resolves. Both platforms select plugins through its `resolveRecipePluginCids`; no production caller reaches `resolveSurfaceRecipe`. Owed: the node and browser compose sites resolve through the one function at surface mount; the wiki door (`mountWiki`), its retained mount specs and the recipe watch retire with the last caller; a surface island's events reach a verb gate bound to its session (`onSurfaceEvent`) when the node callers move (`F4`). O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:594:* `F6` The browser holder as owner, with unicast replies. Slice one stands (PR #56): a closed routing table (`holder-routes.ts`) sends each island message to exactly one port, a reply by its request id, camera traffic by its lease, the island's own asks to its owner port, and drops a kind with no route by name. Slice two stands (PR #58): every tab-to-holder message rides a random owner epoch, a session and a generation, and the holder refuses a stale or unknown one by name to that port alone; `session:open` with its face waits on `W4`'s face supplier. Slices three and four move the Repo and the daemon kernel into the holder; their sealed writes go to the asker (#/rulings, the asker seals). Slice three stands with `K15` step 3 (PR #81): the holder routes each sealed write to the session that caused it, and Chromium, which exposes no nested Worker inside a SharedWorker, takes the dedicated-worker floor, its swap waiting for the worker's `ready` before it replays the manifest and retiring the crossing it replaces. Slice four stays owed. O1.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:605:* `X0b` The idempotent-by-intent pass, after the founding bake, paralleling the isomorphic-by-intent law (operator, 2026-10-19): a replay, a reboot and a retry land nothing new. Every row names itself by its content or its causal id, never a clock or a counter; every write reads first-writer-wins or merges by its CRDT; every boot reads as a function of its stores; and every multi-step act either completes or re-enters to the same end. Its instrument: N boots, each Archive replayed twice, each verb retried, and the second pass of each adds no head and no row. Each finding before the bake cures as its own bug; its instrument runs once before the bake as a census beside `G37`, so a finding that renames a persisted row lands inside the bake, and this pass sweeps what remains. X.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:609:* `X5` The departure walks, in the dress rehearsal, each on synthetic names and each recording the words the display gives at its incomplete crossing: a wiki closed over a refused save (`G33`); a browser profile reopened on the Archives it kept (`B1`); a public reference followed after its author's vessel went dark (`P10`); a command's outcome read through `lares receipt` after its caller gave up. X.
