/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:662:* `P20` The carriage gates (`carriage-board.ts`, `vessel-raise.ts`, `nexus-carriage.ts`) count at the head alone, while `lares nexus members` honours anchored ancestry, so the list can show a member a gate does not yet honour. Built (PR #50): the carrier folds read the anchored lineage, and the contract writer cites the carried heads it supersedes across epochs for both families, so an uncarry, a roll and a re-carry read in order. Built (PR #54): a gate verifies a place contract carried across a charter roll in either direction, a newer gate walking the arm's roll anchors and an older gate accepting the presenter's charter epochs only where they extend its held lineage and pass `verifySealLineage`, each failing closed without its proof; the presenter assembles both, and `readBoardPresentation` folds with ancestry. The herm-mesh and mesh-scenarios witnesses join after A's boot roll. The held-out cell `herm-mesh-roll` (PR #57) rolls A's charter between two herm joins after the boot serves, each herm naming its own head, and presents the opening carry at the rolled head twice: under A's own roll anchor it verifies, and under the same anchor parts signed outside the seats it falls silent by place-contract name. P19's cabal half stays parked on `--gate-ancestry`. P.
