/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:802:* ''The shadow at the gates.'' The law of removal's reach stands whole at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/reach">> (operator ruling): four marked edges, two hands, rolls that carry shadows, a ledger that keeps what a reader counted, a consult at every gate, and keys that never outrun standing. <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/what-the-code-holds">> names each part the code holds and each part that stays owed, and this carrier keeps no copy of that list. The cosign door's verdicts and envelope stand ready for train N's door to adopt. The sealed store's key roll subscribes to the seat's roll and lands with its own train.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:811:* ''Sealed-store step 3'': sealed Repo storage values, hydration checked against the session's face, and the fresh base a from-now admission needs. A face's own names ride its persona plane only once that plane's rest seals, so `lares persona sync` carries nothing until this step lands. It waits on a production session signer (the wire cutover's caller) and on ONE FACE (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/sealed-store#/owed">>).
