/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:47:# Bring every ruling #/open names to the operator before a lane builds against it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:49:!!! Instruments ~ run each fresh before trusting a reading
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:62:!!! Steps
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:63:# `export LAR_ROOT=/tmp/lar-scratch-<you>` before any in-tree boot or any `lares` command that touches the store. `LAR_ROOT` moves the store, the bags root and every projection mirror root; `LAR_BAGS` alone moves only the bags root, and the projection still writes the tracked `bags/` and `wikis/`. A staged e2e vessel takes its own scratch `LAR_ROOT` and no global `LAR_BAGS`. One `lares meme normalize|check` reads files and needs only a scratch `LAR_BAGS`.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:64:# `LAR_ROOT` leaves these homes where they stand: `~/.mempalace` (the destructive `mempalace repave` among its readers), `~/.venv`, `~/.local/bin`, and the harness homes `~/.claude`, `~/.codex`, `~/.copilot`. A `vessel stand --codex` under a scratch root still writes the operator's real harness home.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:65:# Build: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` only where a lead approved an install, then `pnpm -r build`, then `pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:tw5-vendor` (the TW5 core blob that `head-parity` and the plugin smoke need), then `node tools/stamp-build.mjs`. A fresh `git worktree` holds empty submodules; populate them before building there.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:66:# ''A founding wants a human route on a TTY.'' With no TTY it refuses `CredentialTtyRefusal`, and no flag or environment variable carries a credential. A harness founds through the test door: `tools/test-scratch-marker.mjs` stages the root, `tools/seed-test-custody.mjs` names the published test route, then `lares vessel found --skip-build`; `tools/unlock-test-custody.mjs` opens a marked scratch root. An agent may read vessel state and hand the operator the next founding command as text; the operator performs each founding and custody act.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:67:# ''Every boot rests at the floor.'' A verb that needs sovereign state refuses at a standing floor and names `lares vault unlock`. A harness that reads the first `gate key:` line of a log reads the carriage relay's key where a relay stands.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:68:# ''The container'': `tools/lares-container.sh` offers `up`, `down`, `found` and `logs` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor">>). ''The browser surface'': `tools/browser-ci.sh` over `docker-compose.browser-ci.yml`, one project and image tag per builder (`BROWSER_CI_PROJECT`, `BROWSER_CI_IMAGE`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:69:# The tw5 plugin bundle (`packages/lararium-tw5/plugins/lares-memetic-wikitext.json`, `plugins/standalone/*`, `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`) rides in git and must equal a fresh build: rebuild after any tw5 source or tiddler change and commit it with the change. CI's `build-freshness` job checks it. `genesis/` carries that bundle, the boot shadows and the engine blob by address, and the wiki inside a founded vessel runs the bytes genesis carries; a bake (`pnpm --filter @lararium/node build:genesis`) lands as its own labelled `GENESIS RE-BAKE` commit with the CAS change, and a vessel founded on the earlier seed re-founds. `tools/genesis-parity-witness.sh` reads the gap: a bundle that runs ahead of genesis reads red until a bake closes it or a row in `genesis/unbaked.json` declares it.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:70:# `lares-cli` `tests/pour-repave.test.ts` needs the dev-root marker (`LAR_DEV_REPO_ROOT=1` or the ignored `lar-dev-root.json`).
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:71:# Crew shape: the work swarm, one Sonnet Episkopos with one Sol and one Copilot `gpt-5.3-codex` seat, the Opus controller reading every chunk (its seats and the fallback stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">> #/the-shapes), five rounds per set at most, and the solo chain runs beside as many side lanes as hold disjoint files. A builder returns a patch on a narrow one-module brief; the lead applies, builds, tests and commits in its own worktree, then lands whole commits with `git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>` after rebuilding the touched `dist`, since the commit hook runs the built CLI. A lead copies its resume sheet out of the session scratch directory after each commit: a restart empties that directory.
