/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane.mem:52:''MEASURED'' (the code seat, the field seat, and the lead's own read of `face-gate-server.ts`): the dial already runs Noise IK with the dialer's fresh static inside message one, so a dialer already proves itself before the gate sends its verdict. A holder of a candidate responder public key alone cannot test a captured message one (it needs the `es` Diffie-Hellman). The knock (`gateKnock`, an HMAC over the bundle digest, which hashes the whole public pin) tests offline for anyone holding the full candidate pin and an observed path. Any cheap pre-filter keyed on public pin material has that property, WireGuard's `mac1` included (paper section 5.4.4); a pinned dialer holds exactly the public pin, so no filter can tell it from an observer holding the same pin. A filter an observer lacks needs a client-held secret outside the pin, which changes the admission and pinning model.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane.mem:54:''MEASURED'': the knock also selects the gate. The dispatcher registers each Nexus and route at an exact `<route>/<knock>` path; a knock-less dial needs another clear selector or a trial decryption against every gate on a route, and each trial costs one X25519.
/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane.mem:58:''The ruling'' (operator, 2026-10-26): the public knock stays on both tiers, and the leak stands named in `face-proof#/named-leaks`. The measured bound: a reader holding candidate sovereign pins learns which Nexus a dial selects among the K gates behind one address and route, at most log2(K) bits per dial and none where K=1; it learns no face, no verdict and no sealed byte. The pins stand as tests in `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/gate-knock-named-leak.test.ts`, so a silent change to the knock reads red. Option B, a secret selector, lost on cost: it needs per-Nexus key delivery, a causal re-key to every remaining device on each removal, and a first-dial exception, and it protects only later visit timelines where K exceeds one. A public first dial with secret later dials reads as a dual mode. More research stays owed later; the road's `W10` row names when.
